module contract;

// Fluent Bit input-instance total chunk size — resource-projection vocabulary v1.
//
// Card W31-CORPUS-CONTRACTS-2. ONE TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about one upstream
// function. This module verifies nothing: the C body is not analyzed by this
// loader, and a declaration is a premise. Any verdict that rests on it is a
// verdict RELATIVE TO this declaration, never a proof of the C implementation.
//
// The body was read at Fluent Bit
// `66910c10a4d7eafa810b84229cf2dcf7b0f26f97` and is cited by line. The C
// declaration in force is `include/fluent-bit/flb_input_chunk.h:174`:
//
//     size_t flb_input_chunk_total_size(struct flb_input_instance *in);
//
// `size_t` resolves to `unsigned long` on the LP64 model the audited targets
// use, so `usize` is an admissible spelling of the result under the
// declared-ABI agreement gate (standing constraint 8); the parameter is one
// object-pointer level, spelled `ptr<mut, u8>` as every object pointer of this
// vocabulary is. Note the receiver is the input INSTANCE, not an input chunk —
// this is the aggregate query over the instance's stream.
//
// ## `flb_input_chunk_total_size`, read from `src/flb_input_chunk.c:2947-2955`
//
//     size_t flb_input_chunk_total_size(struct flb_input_instance *in)
//     {
//         size_t total = 0;
//         struct flb_storage_input *storage;
//
//         storage = (struct flb_storage_input *) in->storage;
//         total = cio_stream_size_chunks_up(storage->stream);
//         return total;
//     }
//
// That is the whole body: one field read (through a cast the projection
// cannot model but this READING can — the cast reinterprets a `void *` field,
// it neither allocates nor releases), one call, one scalar return. The one
// callee was read too:
//
//   * `cio_stream_size_chunks_up(storage->stream)`
//     (`lib/chunkio/include/chunkio/cio_stream.h:41`;
//     `lib/chunkio/src/cio_stream.c:258-276`) walks the stream's `chunks_up`
//     list with `mk_list_foreach`/`mk_list_entry` (pointer arithmetic, no
//     allocation), calls `cio_chunk_get_content_size` on each chunk — the
//     read-only query `chunkio/chunk_sizes.qcore` declares on this same card,
//     read at `lib/chunkio/src/cio_chunk.c:315-334`: an error-field reset and
//     backend length-field reads, nothing allocated, freed or stored — and
//     sums the non-negative results into a local. Nothing is allocated, freed,
//     stored or published on any path of either body.
//
// This module resolves the size-query member of card W29-CORPUS-CONTRACTS'
// named non-declaration `W29-SIZE-SIBLINGS-UNDECLARED` for exactly one
// sibling: that follow-on's stated reason was that each sibling needs its own
// body reading because several mutate residency state. This one does NOT — the
// reading above finds no residency transition, no `cio_chunk_up`/`down`, no
// list relink — so the obstruction dissolves for this callee, and the
// declaration rests on this module's own reading rather than on its declared
// neighbours' shape (the unfaithful-declaration defect card P07 recorded is
// exactly what this sentence exists to rule out).
//
// ## Which mode is faithful
//
// On every path the caller keeps exactly the obligations it had before the
// call: `resource_borrowed(in)` states that, and it is the only v1 parameter
// mode with that caller-side effect (`owned` demands live custody, `consumed`
// transfers, `released` discharges, `out` creates custody at a destination,
// `stored` transfers under an owner and `removed` detaches from one). The
// walked chunks' error-field resets are writes into the instance's own object
// graph and move no custody, exactly as `input_chunk_write_header`'s writes
// through `chunk` did not (`fluent_bit/input_chunk_helpers.qcore`).
//
// The RESULT is a byte count, a value with no identity:
// `resource_return_none()`.
//
// The declaration says nothing about `in` being non-null — the body
// dereferences it unconditionally, but `resource_borrowed` imposes NO non-null
// precondition, which is the weaker statement and deliberately so: a mode that
// demanded entry custody would delete the caller's failure paths. This is the
// same position `fluent_bit/input_chunk_sizes.qcore` records for its two
// receivers.
//
// ## Why this function is declared although the analysed unit defines it
//
// `src/flb_input_chunk.c` is itself a unit of the pinned corpus, so this is
// the arrangement cards PROD-CONTRACTS, NEIGHBOURS,
// ADDRESS-OF-MEMBER-DESTROY-UNDECLARED, AOM-DESTROY-SIBLINGS and
// W29-CORPUS-CONTRACTS already established: a declared contract ALWAYS wins
// over a W4-inferred summary, a disagreement is reported as a
// `SummaryConflict` diagnostic and never silently resolved
// (`crates/qcore-c-gateway/src/legacy_summary.rs`), and declaring a defined
// function does not stop the unit analysing that function's own body — it
// only fixes what its CALLERS may assume.
//
// ## NOT CLAIMED, recorded rather than hidden
//
//   * **Nothing about the returned value's meaning.** Chunks whose content
//     size reports non-positive are skipped by the summing loop; whether the
//     total is exact is value semantics, outside a custody projection.
//   * **Nothing about which chunks are up.** Membership of `chunks_up` is
//     chunk-residency state (`chunkio/chunk_residency.qcore` declares the
//     explicit residency entry points; this module declares nothing about
//     residency).
//   * **Nothing about retention.** Whether any other object holds `in` or its
//     interior pointers is the unmodeled retention this corpus records as
//     B03/R13 and is not decided here.
//   * **The remaining size siblings stay undeclared.**
//     `flb_input_chunk_is_up`, `flb_input_chunk_set_up` and
//     `input_chunk_metadata_view` were each read on this card and are NOT
//     declared here — the first two are residency wrappers whose faithful
//     declarations exist but belong with the residency family's own module,
//     and the third publishes a borrowed view of the chunk's mapped metadata
//     through an out-parameter, a shape the v1 vocabulary has nowhere to
//     carry. Named `W31-SIZE-SIBLINGS-REMAINDER` in the card report.

// --- the instance's total enqueued bytes, summed over its up chunks ---------
extern fn flb_input_chunk_total_size(in: ptr<mut, u8>) -> usize
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(in);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
